# Feature Engineering Standards

## Feature Categories (from settings.py)

Always import feature lists from config:

```python
from config.settings import (
    EFFICIENCY_FEATURES,    # KADJ EM, KADJ O, KADJ D, BARTHAG, etc.
    FOUR_FACTORS_OFF,       # EFG%, TOV%, OREB%, FTR
    FOUR_FACTORS_DEF,       # EFG%D, TOV%D, DREB%, FTRD
    MODEL_FEATURES,         # Final feature set for models
)
```

## Derived Features

```python
# SEED_STRENGTH: Higher = better seed (1-seed gets 16, 16-seed gets 1)
df['SEED_STRENGTH'] = 17 - df['SEED']

# EM_X_SOS: Efficiency × Schedule Strength interaction
df['EM_X_SOS'] = df['KADJ EM'] * df['ELITE SOS']
```

## Scaling Requirements

```python
from sklearn.preprocessing import StandardScaler

# ✅ Fit scaler on TRAINING data only
scaler = StandardScaler()
X_train_scaled = scaler.fit_transform(X_train)
X_test_scaled = scaler.transform(X_test)  # transform only!

# ❌ Never fit on test data
scaler.fit_transform(X_test)  # LEAKAGE!
```

## Missing Value Strategy

```python
# Check for missing before model training
missing = df[MODEL_FEATURES].isnull().sum()
if missing.any():
    logger.warning(f"Missing values:\n{missing[missing > 0]}")
    
# Imputation options:
# 1. Drop rows (if few missing)
# 2. Median imputation (for numeric)
# 3. Investigate data source (preferred)
```

## Adding New Features

1. Add to appropriate list in `config/settings.py`
2. Implement calculation in feature builder
3. Verify no data leakage (pre-tournament only!)
4. Run backtest to measure impact
